IMPORT prelude

-- Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
-- The Act's fixed days are in s 2: 1 December 2024 (s 2(1)) and 1 July 2025 (s 2(2)). The complaint periods it sets
-- in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 are counted in whole years from the day of the alleged contravention (former
-- s 138: 1 year; new s 138: 2 years), to the same day of the month that many years on (forks F9, F10 in NOTES.md).
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- A Gregorian leap year.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF m EQUALS 2
        THEN IF `leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
        IF (m EQUALS 4) OR (m EQUALS 6) OR (m EQUALS 9) OR (m EQUALS 11)
        THEN 30
        OTHERWISE 31

-- The day a number of whole years after a day: the same day of the month, that many years on; where that month has no
-- such day (29 February in a common year), the last day of that month (fork F10).
GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `the years` `years after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the year reached`
    WHERE
        `the year reached` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `the years`
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the number of days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the year reached`
            THEN `the number of days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the year reached`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`
